# golang.override — explicit Go-toolchain exceptions for resolve-go.sh
#
# Normally EMPTY. The Go version is read from each teleport tag's own source
# (build.assets/versions.mk|Makefile GOLANG_VERSION/RUNTIME, or the v2 Dockerfile),
# so it matches what upstream shipped. Add a line here ONLY when that extracted
# version cannot be built (e.g. the exact old Go is no longer reproducible) and you
# need to pin a deliberate substitute. Values are also subject to the GVM compile
# ceiling in resolve-go.sh (use <= 1.23; toolchain auto-download handles newer).
#
# Format (most-specific wins): vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH,go_version
#                              vMAJOR.MINOR,go_version
#                              vMAJOR,go_version
# Example: v3.1.18,1.13
#
# (no overrides currently)
